{"acceptedResponses":["E"],"answer":"E","bank":"amc","batch":"NA","choiceOrder":["A","B","C","D","E"],"choices":{"A":"\\(-12\\)","B":"\\(-6\\)","C":"\\(0\\)","D":"\\(6\\)","E":"\\(12\\)"},"choicesType":"text","domain":[],"editorialNote":"","figureSources":{},"id":"1986_AMC_12_Q13","knowledgeGraph":{"assessedIds":["cnm_233"],"contentHash":"9705fd5786d94260d438b71da432195a83d49d539cd9db8f72289dedd1712f3d","flags":[],"reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"use-vertex-form","label":"Vertex form","methodDirectNodeIds":{"use-vertex-form":["cnm_231","cnm_042","cnm_148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_231","cnm_042","cnm_148"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"solve-general-coefficients","label":"General-form coefficients","methodDirectNodeIds":{"solve-general-coefficients":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_029","cnm_042"],"id":"use-the-vertex-form","label":"Use the given vertex","methodDirectNodeIds":{"use-the-vertex-form":["cnm_233","cnm_231","cnm_148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_233","cnm_231","cnm_148","cnm_029","cnm_042"]}],"status":"mapped","supportIds":["cnm_029"],"version":"1.0.0"},"level":"AMC 12","number":13,"question":"A parabola \\(y=ax^2+bx+c\\) has vertex \\((4,2).\\) If \\((2,0)\\) is on the parabola, then \\(abc\\) equals","questionType":"text","rejectedAnswers":[],"responseType":"choice","schemaVersion":"3.0","skill":[],"solution":"The vertex \\((4,2)\\) lets us write the parabola in vertex form with only its scale factor unknown:\n\\[\ny=a(x-4)^2+2,\n\\qquad a\\ne0.\n\\]\nSince \\((2,0)\\) lies on the parabola,\n\\[\n0=a(2-4)^2+2=4a+2,\n\\]\nso \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\). Expanding identifies the coefficients in the requested general form:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-\\frac12(x^2-8x+16)+2\\\\\n&=-\\frac12x^2+4x-6.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\), \\(b=4\\), and \\(c=-6\\), giving\n\\[\nabc=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)(4)(-6)=12.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).","solutionAvailability":"present","solutionMethods":[{"directNodeIds":["cnm_233","cnm_231","cnm_148"],"explanation":"The vertex \\((4,2)\\) lets us write the parabola in vertex form with only its scale factor unknown:\n\\[\ny=a(x-4)^2+2,\n\\qquad a\\ne0.\n\\]\nSince \\((2,0)\\) lies on the parabola,\n\\[\n0=a(2-4)^2+2=4a+2,\n\\]\nso \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\). Expanding identifies the coefficients in the requested general form:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-\\frac12(x^2-8x+16)+2\\\\\n&=-\\frac12x^2+4x-6.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus \\(a=-\\tfrac12\\), \\(b=4\\), and \\(c=-6\\), giving\n\\[\nabc=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)(4)(-6)=12.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).","id":"use-the-vertex-form","label":"Use the given vertex","legacyRouteId":"use-the-vertex-form","provenance":{"evidence":[{"label":"Accepted primary worked-solution review","path":"../database/knowledge-graph/evidence/solutions-2026-11-06/1986_AMC_12_Q13.json","sha256":"46f48d185a3f258f66e9c6f5c041dd1b914bbb31e188a6b97eaa2b8f27348c14"}],"license":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","reviewStatus":"AI-authored and independently AI-reviewed; not teacher reviewed","source":"Original Math Practice solution","sourceRef":"amc/1986_AMC_12_Q13#use-the-vertex-form","sourceURL":"https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice"}},{"directNodeIds":["cnm_231","cnm_042","cnm_148"],"id":"use-vertex-form","label":"Vertex form","legacyRouteId":"use-vertex-form","provenance":{"evidence":[{"label":"Legacy graph and grading review","path":"../database/knowledge-graph/evidence/solutions-2026-11-06/1986_AMC_12_Q13.json","sha256":"46f48d185a3f258f66e9c6f5c041dd1b914bbb31e188a6b97eaa2b8f27348c14"}],"license":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","source":"Existing reviewed concept route","sourceRef":"amc/1986_AMC_12_Q13#use-vertex-form"}},{"directNodeIds":["cnm_232","cnm_093"],"id":"solve-general-coefficients","label":"General-form coeffici